  "result": "Fixed. `--help` listed each option's names longest-first (`--verbose, -v`). It now puts the short form first (`-v, --verbose`), which is the usual click layout.\n\n- **Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py` sorted option names by prefix length with `reverse=True`. I removed the `reverse=True`.\n- **Option order:** the order of options themselves was already correct (declaration order, with `--help` last).\n- **Tests:** I added two tests to `tests/test_formatting.py`, one for `join_options` directly and one checking `--help` output. The full suite passes (1908 passed, 102 skipped).\n\nIf you meant something other than the order of names within each option, such as the order of the options themselves, tell me what you're seeing and I'll look again.",
